ameter t is a true arc-length parameter because (√3/2)² + (1/2)² = 1.\n\nTherefore\n\n|MN| = |t₁ − t₂| = √((t₁ + t₂)² − 4t₁t₂) = √(48 + 32) = √80 = 4√5.\n\nFinal answer: (Ⅰ) A(4, π/6), B(−4, π/6) (equivalently (4, 7π/6)); (Ⅱ) |MN| = 4√5.","ttft_ms":2373,"type":"result","duration_ms":4683,"uuid":"294a935b-1e05-4b90-8c12-a1c62a3e12c8","ttft_stream_ms":686,"time_to_request_ms":20,"first_content_frame_ms":687,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
